I want you to create a markdown document in this directory how everything works together the software that we build contains of  two different applications basically  one application is running on the machine where the drum player is playing  drums on the Clone hero game and the other is where the guitar player is playing guitar on the Rocksmith game  the software that runs on the drum machine is called drum server it hosts  a  socket server  and allows the guitar player to send a trigger via the guitar client that  then simultaneously starts the song on  the drum machine  and on the guitar machine  so that when the thumbs are measured well  the songs play synchronous and the players can enjoy playing the songs at the same time  to be able to do this both songs needs to be available for both platforms  for the Drum player it's global for the data player it's Rocksmith  to be able to have those songs then being played synchronized,  the important part is to measure  the times  exactly or as good as possible  that  the songs on the differences systems start on the first note  at the same time  for this there is a measurement task needed.  to be able to do this there is another application that is called time measure  time measure works this way that  the guitar or the  drum player  rests in the  screen in the application just before the song starts  then  with pressing a it will  start the song and at the same time start the  timing when then the first note comes  that both players have agreed on to measure  the players need to press q  to make the time measure stop.  then the players share their times and  the guitar player can  add a new a song in the guitar client  while he enters both  time measures from the Drum player and himself as the guitar player into the UI and then press add  when everything works well  the songs are now perfectly synced.  to then play the songs together both players needs to go to the screen that  will start the song on the next button press  the guitar player will select the desired song in the guitar client  and press the hotkey to start  that key press then will  Trigger  the start of the song   on each machine  on the drum machine and the guitar machine so that the songs  are ins sync.   in our setup the Drum player screens it's screen  to the guitar player and the guitar player will  include this screen into his streaming setup while he also shows his screen  the sound will only be taken from the guitar player. therefore there will be some latency in the communication way from the Drum player to the guitar player. That means that we have a static offset in that communication way from the drum player to the guitar player, and we have this individual measurements for the drum player and the guitar player. We need to describe what these different time measures mean. What does it mean when we have a high number for the drum player? What does it mean if we have a higher number for the guitar player?  